+## Optional learnability probe in review-a84488efcfeb33e9
+
+A source-pinned protected-Racket probe found a concrete teaching shortcut.  The
+current generator always places square blocks at columns `1 + k*(N+3)`, so a
+wrong rule can infer band height N and sample those fixed cells without detecting
+solid squares.  It fits three ordinary demonstrations.  Moving the first square
+one column right is still lawful under the canonical rule and preserves its
+answer, but the fixed-slot rule changes one output cell.  Evidence and a reusable
+probe are in `workspace/learnability_probe.py` and
+`checks/dc59d4c62234/learnability-probe.json`.  Suggested repair: vary square
+columns constructively across visible demonstrations while preserving order and
+non-overlap.  This is one finite shortcut finding, not a complete ambiguity audit.
+The new task-local tests execute the probe and generator contract; the staged
+selected suite now passes 2/2.  An earlier no-tests exit 5 is retained in checks
+as the red state that motivated adding coverage.
